        <div id="how-much-protein-do-runners-need" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. How Much Protein Do Runners Need?
          </h2>

          <p>
            The 2016 joint position statement from the American College of Sports Medicine, the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics and Dietitians of Canada recommends 1.2 to 2.0 g of protein per kilogram of body weight per day for athletes, including endurance athletes. The International Society of Sports Nutrition's 2017 position stand lands in a similar place, suggesting 1.4 to 2.0 g/kg for most exercising people. Research using the indicator amino acid oxidation method in endurance-trained athletes (Kato and colleagues, 2016) estimated needs on a training day at about 1.65 g/kg on average, with a recommended intake closer to 1.8 g/kg.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
